These are test keys for GPG key update/rotation testing. They include
secret keys. Use these for testing GPG key updates (new subkeys, expiry
changes, revocations, cross-signed key rotation). Do *NOT* ever use
these for any real application.

Generated by tests/generate-test-gpg-keys.sh.

Key inventory:
  primary-a.gpg / primary-a.sec.gpg     — Base key A (signing + cert)
  primary-a-newsubkey.gpg                — Key A with additional signing subkey
  primary-a-newsubkey.sec.gpg            — Secret key for signing with new subkey
  primary-a-extended.gpg                 — Key A with expiration extended to 2035
  primary-a-revoked.gpg                  — Key A with primary revocation applied
  primary-a-revokedsubkey.gpg            — Key A with initial subkey revoked
  primary-b-old.gpg / primary-b-old.sec.gpg — Old trusted primary for rotation tests
  primary-b-new.sec.gpg                  — New primary B secret key
  primary-b-new-crosssigned.gpg          — New primary cross-signed by B-old (positive test)
  primary-b-new-unsigned.gpg             — New primary WITHOUT cross-signature (negative test)
  primary-b-new-selfsigned.gpg           — New primary only self-signed (negative test)
  unrelated.gpg                          — Completely unrelated key (negative test)
  key-ids.txt                            — Key fingerprints and IDs
